    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0372" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p1/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845C.191 BU/7–853: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Eisenhower to the Governor of Southern
                        Rhodesia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d138-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-10T11:07:00-04:00">July 10, 1953—11:07
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I wish to acknowledge the receipt of your very gracious message stating that you
                    and your Ministers would welcome a visit by a representative of the United
                    States Government to the Rhodes Centenary Exhibition at Bulawayo.</p>
                <p>It gives me great pleasure to accept, on behalf of this Government, your kind
                    invitation and to inform you that I have designated Mr. William H. Ball of
                    Muncie, Indiana, to attend the Exhibition as my Special Representative, with the
                    personal rank of Minister.</p>
                <p>I shall convey to Mr. Ball the generous invitation that he stay with you and Lady
                    Kennedy at Government House in Bulawayo from August 5 to 8 and of your
                    willingness to arrange a tour of Southern Rhodesia for him.</p>
                <p>Please accept my sincere thanks for your personal message of greetings and good
                    wishes which I most heartily reciprocate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight P.
                    Eisenhower</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d138-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d138-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was drafted by Durnan of AF and Muir of S/S–PR and cleared by the
                    White House.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
